Bound recursion on wasm32 (and in --cfg fuzzing builds): decline past 2048

Native checking runs on 2 GiB thread stacks and has no recursion limit. On
wasm32 guest calls run on the engine's native stack (wasmfuzz: 8 MiB for
run-input, 32 MiB per fuzzing worker), so deep evaluation would end in a
stack-overflow trap instead of a verdict. A Nest guard at the recursive
steps (eval_node, apply_new, whnf_head_uncached, value_type_uncached,
unify_general, infer_nonvar, bignum_via_force) counts their nesting and declines
(unsupported!) past MAX_NEST = 2048. Native builds without --cfg fuzzing
compile the guard to nothing.
Upstream: none (no related issue or PR; issues #2-#12 are soundness, OOM and
loose-bvar reports, checked 2026-11-22).

